.\" pmconfigd(8) — NextBSD power management daemon.
.\"
.\" NextBSD-original. Apple ships no manual page for powerd.
.\"
.Dd November 3, 2026
.Dt PMCONFIGD 8
.Os NextBSD
.Sh NAME
.Nm pmconfigd
.Nd power management daemon
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm
is Apple's power management daemon, built from PowerManagement-1846.120.8.0.1
(macOS installs it as
.Pa powerd ) .
It owns power policy: power assertions, idle and display sleep, power
sources, and the system sleep and wake sequence.
.Pp
It is started by
.Xr launchd 8
as the job
.Ql org.nextbsd.powerd
and is not intended to be run by hand.
It vends the two Mach services Apple's IOKit power management client code
looks up:
.Bl -tag -width "com.apple.PowerManagement.control"
.It Ql com.apple.PowerManagement.control
the MIG interface of
.In IOKit/pwr_mgt/IOPMLib.h ,
.In IOKit/pwr_mgt/IOPMLibPrivate.h
and
.In IOKit/ps/IOPowerSources.h .
.It Ql com.apple.iokit.powerdxpc
the XPC interface used for asynchronous assertions and user activity.
.El
.Pp
The daemon is being ported in stages.
In this release it checks in both services and keeps the system's
scheduled power events
.Po
.Xr pmset 1
.Cm schedule
and
.Cm repeat ,
.Fn IOPMSchedulePowerEvent
and
.Fn IOPMScheduleRepeatingPowerEvent
.Pc .
When a scheduled
.Cm shutdown
or
.Cm restart
comes due,
.Nm
asks
.Xr launchd 8
to power off or reboot, as
.Xr shutdown 8
does.
A scheduled
.Cm sleep
asks the kernel's power management root domain to sleep the machine; it
is logged and not performed where the machine cannot sleep.
.Cm wake
and
.Cm poweron
events are kept and listed, but no hardware alarm is set for them yet, so
they do not wake or power on the machine.
.Pp
.Nm
is a client of the kernel's power management root domain, the
.Ql IOPMrootDomain
registry entry, which it reaches through
.Pa /dev/iopmroot .
The root domain runs every system sleep and wake and waits for its clients'
answers;
.Nm
answers it, and passes each sleep and wake on to the processes registered
through
.Fn IOPMConnectionCreate ,
holding the sleep until they acknowledge it or 28 seconds pass.
It posts
.Ql com.apple.powermanagement.systempowerstate
.Pq Xr notify 3
at each sleep and wake.
.Pp
While it runs,
.Nm
owns the lid and power button policy, and the kernel's own
.Va hw.acpi.lid_switch_state ,
.Va hw.acpi.power_button_state
and
.Va hw.acpi.sleep_button_state
actions are off: closing the lid sleeps the system
.Pq Dq Clamshell Sleep ,
and so does the power button
.Pq Dq Power Button Sleep .
When the battery reaches its critical level while the system runs on it,
.Nm
sleeps the system
.Pq Dq Low Power Sleep .
When
.Nm
exits, the kernel's ACPI actions apply again.
.Pp
.Nm
keeps the system's power assertions
.Po
.Xr caffeinate 8 ,
.Fn IOPMAssertionCreateWithName
.Pc
and applies them as macOS does:
.Bl -tag -width "PreventUserIdleDisplaySleep"
.It Ql PreventUserIdleSystemSleep
holds off idle sleep;
.It Ql PreventUserIdleDisplaySleep
holds off display sleep, and so idle sleep too;
.It Ql PreventSystemSleep
holds off idle sleep as a CPU assertion in the root domain.
.El
.Pp
The Energy Saver settings
.Po
the
.Cm sleep
and
.Cm displaysleep
minutes and the rest
.Pc
are Apple's defaults
.Pq 10 and 10 minutes on AC power
merged with the settings saved in the
.Ql com.apple.PowerManagement
preferences, and are re-read when
.Ql com.apple.system.powermanagement.prefschange
is posted.
After
.Cm displaysleep
minutes without user input the display is considered off; after
.Cm sleep
minutes without input the system is asked to sleep with the reason
.Ql Idle Sleep ,
which lets any application veto it.
The time of the last input comes from the
.Ql HIDIdleTime
of the
.Ql IOHIDSystem
registry entry; while there is none, the user counts as active and the
system does not idle-sleep.
Active remote logins
.Pq Xr ssh 1
hold off idle sleep while their terminals are in use.
.Pp
Every other MIG request is answered with
.Dv kIOReturnUnsupported ;
XPC messages are accepted and ignored.
.Sh FILES
.Bl -tag -width "/System/Library/LaunchDaemons/org.nextbsd.powerd.plist" -compact
.It Pa /System/Library/LaunchDaemons/org.nextbsd.powerd.plist
the
.Xr launchd 8
job
.It Pa /Local/Library/Preferences/SystemConfiguration/com.apple.AutoWake.plist
the scheduled and repeating power events
.It Pa /System/Library/CoreServices/powerd.bundle
Apple's assertion timeout and category lists
.It Pa /dev/iopmroot
the kernel's power management root domain
.It Pa /var/log/pmconfigd.stderr
the daemon's log
.El
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr launchctl 1 ,
.Xr pmset 1 ,
.Xr notify 3 ,
.Xr caffeinate 8 ,
.Xr launchd 8 ,
.Xr shutdown 8
.Sh HISTORY
.Nm
first appeared in NextBSD in 2026.
